course: dictionary
lesson: 2955
title: One word, two meanings: drizzle
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Drizzle can be a noun or a verb. As a noun, a drizzle is light rain. As a verb, to drizzle means to rain lightly, so «it's drizzling» means the rain is weak but still wet. Read the words around the word to find out which meaning fits.
explain: Look at this context: «stratus are flat grey sheets that may bring drizzle.» Stratus clouds are flat and grey, and grey clouds can bring rain, so drizzle must be a light, grey kind of rain. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Light rain would fit, and it makes sense in the sentence.
explain: Drizzle is also a cooking word. In a recipe, «drizzle with olive oil» means pour a thin stream of oil over the food. The weather meaning is about rain, and the cooking meaning is about pouring something thinly. The clues in the sentence tell you which one you need.
fact: Drizzle is light rain falling in very small, fine drops.
fact: To drizzle means to rain lightly, as in «it's drizzling».
fact: In cooking, to drizzle means to pour a thin stream of liquid, such as honey or oil, over food.
fact: Stratus clouds are flat grey sheets that may bring drizzle.
fact: Drizzle is a weak rain, much lighter than the heavy rain and thunder of a storm.
exercise: In «a light drizzle», what is falling? | Big hailstones | *Very fine drops of rain | Thick snow | Hot sand
exercise: «Stratus are flat grey sheets that may bring drizzle.» What kind of cloud is a stratus? | A thin wisp of ice high up | A towering storm cloud | A white puffy heap | *A flat grey sheet of cloud
exercise: In a recipe, «drizzle with olive oil» means to | Cook the food in a big pan of oil | *Pour a thin stream of oil over the food | Throw oil at the food | Wash the food in oil
test: «It's drizzling, so take a coat.» What is happening outside? | Heavy thunder | *Light rain falling | Bright sunshine | Hail
test: Which cloud brings heavy rain, thunder and sometimes hail? | Cumulus | Stratus | Cirrus | *Cumulonimbus
exam: A recipe says «drizzle with honey». What should you do? | Dip the food in honey | Put the honey in the oven | Stir in honey until it is thick | *Pour a thin stream of honey over the food
